From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: contributor <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvapi: optional low-overhead latency-marker trace

Adds an env-gated (DXVK_NVAPI_LATENCY_MARKER_TRACE=1) trace in
NvAPI_D3D_SetLatencyMarker that emits one compact line per Reflex marker
(frameID, marker type, QPC microseconds), prefixed "LAT".

This is a markers-only alternative to DXVK_NVAPI_LOG_LEVEL=trace, which logs
*every* NvAPI call (thousands of lines/sec). Logging only latency markers
(hundreds/sec) lets an external reader derive sim-to-present latency without
the full-trace overhead.

It is also useful on Linux/Proton where vkd3d-proton clears the Reflex
low-latency swapchain owner once frame generation creates a second Vulkan
swapchain: the in-band SIMULATION_START/PRESENT_END markers then never reach
a Vulkan layer, but remain observable here.

Pure observation; no behavior change when the env var is unset.
diff --git a/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp b/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
index 1ea406c..6eefb76 100644
--- a/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
+++ b/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
@@ -369,6 +369,25 @@ NVAPI_FUNCTION NvAPI_D3D_SetLatencyMarker(IUnknown* pDev, NV_LATENCY_MARKER_PARA
         return Ok(n, alreadyLoggedOk);
     }
 
+    // Optional low-overhead latency-marker trace (env-gated, observation only):
+    // emit one line per Reflex marker (frameID, marker type, monotonic
+    // microseconds). Unlike full trace logging this is markers-only, so an
+    // external reader can derive latency without the full-trace overhead. It
+    // also captures the in-band markers above any swapchain-level gating.
+    static const bool latencyMarkerTrace =
+        env::getEnvVariable("DXVK_NVAPI_LATENCY_MARKER_TRACE") == "1";
+    if (latencyMarkerTrace) {
+        LARGE_INTEGER ticks, freq;
+        ::QueryPerformanceCounter(&ticks);
+        ::QueryPerformanceFrequency(&freq);
+        auto us = static_cast<uint64_t>(
+            (static_cast<double>(ticks.QuadPart) / static_cast<double>(freq.QuadPart)) * 1e6);
+        log::info(str::format(
+            "LAT frame=", pSetLatencyMarkerParams->frameID,
+            " marker=", static_cast<uint32_t>(pSetLatencyMarkerParams->markerType),
+            " t_us=", us));
+    }
+
     switch (lowLatencyDevice->SetLatencyMarker(pSetLatencyMarkerParams->frameID, markerType.value())) {
         case S_OK:
             return Ok(n, alreadyLoggedOk);
